*Diagram to be drawn by the candidate.* Draw a large **side view (sagittal section) of the human brain**, about half a page, with clean continuous lines and labelling lines that do not cross. It must show and label:

- the **cerebrum** (cerebral hemispheres), the largest part, with its folded surface (**cerebral cortex**, gyri and sulci);
- the **corpus callosum** joining the two hemispheres (in a section);
- the **thalamus** and **hypothalamus** below it, with the **pituitary gland** attached to the hypothalamus;
- the **cerebellum**, at the back below the cerebrum, with a branching pattern;
- the **pons (Pons varolii)** in front of the cerebellum;
- the **medulla oblongata**, which continues downwards as the **spinal cord**;
- optionally the **meninges** around the brain and the **olfactory lobe**.

Give a **title** ("Diagram of the mammalian (human) brain, side view") and draw labelling lines with a ruler. Marks are given for size, neatness, accuracy and labels.
